course: dictionary
lesson: 4650
title: Many meanings, one word: hit
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word hit is short, but it has many meanings. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning is right. «A car turned towards him, and it hit him» means the car struck him hard and fast.
explain: Read the sentence and ask what fits. «The song was a big hit» does not mean anyone was struck. Big and song are your clues: a hit here means something very popular.
explain: Hit can also mean reach a goal or target. «She hit the target» means her arrow or ball landed on it. Try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you probably have the right one.
fact: Hit is a verb and a noun: you can hit a ball, or you can have a hit.
fact: «Hit» can mean to touch or strike something hard and fast, or to bump into something by accident.
fact: «A hit» can mean a very popular song, film or thing.
fact: «The storm hit the town» means the storm struck suddenly. Hit can also mean to reach a number, as in «hit 100».
fact: Hitting another person is never okay, even when you are angry. Walk away, and tell an adult.
exercise: «A car turned towards him, and it hit him and broke his leg.» What does hit mean here? | A very popular song | To say hello politely | *To strike or bump into something hard | To reach a target
exercise: «The song was a big hit.» What does hit mean here? | A hard blow with a fist | To miss the target | A sudden storm | *A very popular song
exercise: «The diggers must not hit the cables under the pavement.» What does hit mean here? | To be very popular | To reach midnight | To say sorry | *To bump into or damage something by accident
test: «She hit the target with her arrow.» Which meaning fits best? | A sad, grey day | *To reach a goal or mark | To sing loudly | To run away quickly
test: Ella says hit always means to punch someone. What is the best reply? | Yes, and punching is fine | Yes, it only ever means to punch | *No, hit has many meanings, and context shows which one | No, it means to go to sleep
exam: When you meet hit in a sentence, what should you do first? | Look it up and stop reading | Guess the first meaning you think of | Skip the sentence forever | *Read the words around it and try a meaning that fits
